From: Illia Komsa <ik@fungamer.co>
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: cut the CSS parser's allocation churn

Parsing the user-agent sheet on the first style update allocated 16.5 MB
for 2.3 MB kept. The syntax parser now sizes its vectors before filling
them: component-value lists, preludes, declaration runs and block contents
are counted with a token walk (count_component_values,
Parser::count_block_items) and reserved once, rounded up to a power of two
so they stay in the few allocator size classes the regrown vectors used.
The token vector is sized from the input without its comments (a third of
the UA sheet). SourcePosition is 32-bit (tokens 128 -> 112 bytes). A
stylesheet's top-level rules go to SyntaxParseBuilder one at a time, so
each rule's syntax tree is freed before the next is built. The counter
style `symbols` and `additive-symbols` descriptors and component_list_source
reserve their output instead of collecting through size-hint-less
iterators.

Empty page, load -> render-0: 16.5 -> 11.5 MB allocated, freed-not-purged
mimalloc pages 2.33 -> 1.45 MB.

